# ds-worker configuration
#
# Copy to ~/.config/ds-worker/config (install.sh does this for you if it is
# missing) and uncomment what you want to change. Every value here is a default:
# an environment variable of the same name always wins, so you can still
# override per call:
#
#   DS_MODEL_REVIEWER=gx10/qwen3.8-flash-next ds-worker reviewer "..."
#
# This file is PARSED, not sourced. Only the keys listed below are read, values
# are taken literally, and nothing here is executed. No $(...), no variables.
# Check what is actually in effect with:  ds-doctor --config

# --- models -----------------------------------------------------------------
# See what this machine has:  opencode models | grep local-vllm
#
# Each role has a PRIMARY model and a FALLBACK model. ds-worker tries the
# primary up to DS_MODEL_RETRIES times, and only after all of those fail does
# it move to the fallback for up to DS_MODEL_RETRIES more tries — stopping at
# the first success. --model on a single call bypasses this chain entirely
# and runs exactly that model once. For the writing `worker` role, the chain
# only continues to the next attempt while --dir is a git working tree
# confirmed unchanged since the chain started (see references/verification.md, "Safety model").
#
# Built-in default (no config needed): local GX10 DeepSeek on the single `local-vllm`
# provider (:8000), 2 tries, no fallback — no external API, no per-call
# billing, no rate limit. The box serves one model at a time, so there is no
# second endpoint to fall back to; when the primary is spent the call fails
# outright instead of silently retrying a dead port.

#DS_MODEL_EXPLORER=gx10/qwen3.8-flash-next
#DS_MODEL_REVIEWER=gx10/qwen3.8-flash-next
#DS_MODEL_WORKER=gx10/qwen3.8-flash-next

# Empty by default. Set these only while a second model is genuinely being
# served — a fallback pointing at a model that is not loaded just burns
# DS_MODEL_RETRIES more attempts before failing.
#DS_MODEL_EXPLORER_FALLBACK=
#DS_MODEL_REVIEWER_FALLBACK=
#DS_MODEL_WORKER_FALLBACK=
#DS_MODEL_RETRIES=2

# The critic role runs the doc-critic agent, whose model is bound in the agent's
# own config (cross-model by design — NOT a local GX10 model). Empty = leave it
# to the agent config; set it only to pin a different model deliberately.
#DS_MODEL_CRITIC=

# --- serving-model autodetect ------------------------------------------------
# The box serves ONE model at a time, so the pins above go stale as soon as you
# load a different one. With autodetect on (the default) ds-worker asks the
# endpoint which model is actually loaded and uses that, so swapping DeepSeek
# for Qwen on :8000 needs no config change. It only overrides the pin when the
# loaded model is in the provider's catalog in opencode.jsonc; otherwise it
# keeps the pin and says why. --model always wins over autodetect.
#
# DS_MODEL_ENDPOINT is empty by default, meaning "read the baseURL out of
# opencode.jsonc for this model's provider" — set it only to probe a different
# endpoint than the one the provider is configured with.

#DS_MODEL_AUTODETECT=1
#DS_MODEL_ENDPOINT=

# Pin a specific catalog model instead (disables nothing, but autodetect will
# still redirect it if a different model is loaded — use --model to truly pin):
#DS_MODEL_EXPLORER=gx10/qwen3.8-flash-next
#DS_MODEL_REVIEWER=gx10/qwen3.8-flash-next
#DS_MODEL_WORKER=gx10/qwen3.8-flash-next

# Cloud DeepSeek alternative, if the GX10 box is down or you want a different
# model per role. Measured cost: pro is roughly 3-4x flash. explorer does wide
# mechanical reading and its file:line claims get verified anyway, so it
# defaults to flash; worker writes code, where a plausible-but-wrong edit is
# the expensive failure.
#DS_MODEL_EXPLORER=opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash
#DS_MODEL_REVIEWER=opencode-go/deepseek-v4-pro
#DS_MODEL_WORKER=opencode-go/deepseek-v4-pro

# OpenCode Zen's free tier bills $0 and needs no subscription. Expect rate
# limits under load. Note the -free suffix: `opencode/deepseek-v4-flash` without
# it is not a real model id, and the run fails at dispatch.
#DS_MODEL_EXPLORER=opencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free
#DS_MODEL_REVIEWER=opencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free
#DS_MODEL_WORKER=opencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free

# A key may appear more than once; the last line wins. Copy a block, edit the
# copy, and the earlier one stays as a record of what you moved away from.

# --- execution --------------------------------------------------------------
# DS_IDLE_TIMEOUT  seconds with no OpenCode NDJSON output before exit 124;
#                  reasoning, answer, and tool events all reset this timer;
#                  0 disables this outer idle watchdog
# DS_MAX_RUNTIME   absolute wall-clock limit for one call (exit 124)
# DS_TIMEOUT       legacy alias for DS_MAX_RUNTIME
# DS_SERVE    off = fresh process per call (default), auto = opt-in shared backend
# DS_AUTO     1 = pass --auto. Required for headless runs; it cannot override a
#             `deny` in an agent definition, which is what keeps the read-only
#             roles read-only. Set to 0 only when debugging permission prompts.
# DS_PROGRESS_INTERVAL  seconds between numeric stderr progress reports; 0 disables
# DS_AUTO_RECOVER_READONLY  1 = one session recovery for explorer/reviewer
# DS_RECOVERY_IDLE_TIMEOUT / DS_RECOVERY_MAX_RUNTIME  recovery watchdog limits

#DS_IDLE_TIMEOUT=1200
#DS_MAX_RUNTIME=3600
#DS_TIMEOUT=3600
#DS_PROGRESS_INTERVAL=15
#DS_AUTO_RECOVER_READONLY=1
#DS_RECOVERY_IDLE_TIMEOUT=60
#DS_RECOVERY_MAX_RUNTIME=180
#DS_SERVE=off
#DS_AUTO=1

# --- backend ----------------------------------------------------------------
# DS_OPENCODE_PORT is a starting point. If it is busy (an OpenCode TUI often
# holds 4096), ds-serve scans upward and never attaches to a server it did not
# start. Binding anything other than loopback requires OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD.

#DS_OPENCODE_HOST=127.0.0.1
#DS_OPENCODE_PORT=4096
#DS_PORT_SCAN=20

# --- local reasoning model --------------------------------------------------
# These are OpenCode provider options, not ds-worker config keys. In
# ~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc, set them under the local provider used by
# the selected model. `chunkTimeout` is the gap between streamed SSE chunks;
# `timeout` is the provider request's absolute limit.
#
#   "options": {
#     "chunkTimeout": 60000,
#     "timeout": 1800000
#   }
#
# Restart the owned backend after changing provider options:
#   ds-serve restart

# --- paths ------------------------------------------------------------------
#DS_STATE_DIR=~/.local/state/ds-worker
